{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_030","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"WebAssembly JavaScript interface","location_hint":"paragraph 171","char_start":5974,"char_end":6006,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_031","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"This object acts as the namespace for all WebAssembly-related functionality.","location_hint":"paragraph 172","char_start":6009,"char_end":6085,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_032","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"A WebAssembly.Global object represents a global variable instance, accessible from both JavaScript and importable/exportable across one or more WebAssembly.Module instances. This allows dynamic linking of multiple modules.","location_hint":"paragraph 174","char_start":6111,"char_end":6333,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_033","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"A WebAssembly.Module object contains stateless WebAssembly code that has already been compiled by the browser and can be efficiently shared with Workers , and instantiated multiple times.","location_hint":"paragraph 176","char_start":6359,"char_end":6546,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_034","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"A WebAssembly.Instance object is a stateful, executable instance of a Module . Instance objects contain all the Exported WebAssembly functions that allow calling into WebAssembly code from JavaScript.","location_hint":"paragraph 178","char_start":6574,"char_end":6774,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_035","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"The WebAssembly.compile() function compiles WebAssembly binary code into a WebAssembly.Module object.","location_hint":"paragraph 180","char_start":6801,"char_end":6902,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_036","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"WebAssembly.compileStreaming()","location_hint":"paragraph 181","char_start":6905,"char_end":6935,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_037","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"The WebAssembly.compileStreaming() function compiles a WebAssembly.Module directly from a streamed underlying source.","location_hint":"paragraph 182","char_start":6938,"char_end":7055,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_038","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"The WebAssembly.instantiate() function allows you to compile and instantiate WebAssembly code.","location_hint":"paragraph 184","char_start":7086,"char_end":7180,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_039","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming()","location_hint":"paragraph 185","char_start":7183,"char_end":7217,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_040","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"The WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming() function is the primary API for compiling and instantiating WebAssembly code, returning both a Module and its first Instance .","location_hint":"paragraph 186","char_start":7220,"char_end":7385,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_041","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"The WebAssembly.validate() function validates a given typed array of WebAssembly binary code.","location_hint":"paragraph 188","char_start":7413,"char_end":7506,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_042","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"A WebAssembly.Memory object is a resizable ArrayBuffer that holds the raw bytes of memory accessed by an Instance .","location_hint":"paragraph 190","char_start":7532,"char_end":7647,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_043","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"A WebAssembly.Table object is a resizable typed array of opaque values, like function references, that are accessed by an Instance .","location_hint":"paragraph 192","char_start":7672,"char_end":7804,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_0974a54becd4_044","source_id":"src_0974a54becd4","source_hash":"bc8fb56bddc65e82103061d7276ae3eafae3761671dfdece0f878b89d0c9b276","text":"The WebAssembly.Tag object defines a type of WebAssembly exception that can be thrown to/from WebAssembly code.","location_hint":"paragraph 194","char_start":7827,"char_end":7938,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-10T08:15:01.169Z"}
